Description: Learn metadata on demand in live folder mode
 Live folders now learn details where it is cheap, and keep them in memory
 (an LRU cache in fsmeta.c, checked against each file's size and mtime):
 .
  - Folders with at most probe_limit (30) media files have them probed for
    duration, resolution, bitrate, DLNA profile and tags while the client
    waits, for at most probe_time (500 ms); the rest finishes in the
    background. Larger folders are not probed.
  - A played file is probed in the background and a video gets a thumbnail
    (a frame via ffmpegthumbnailer, or its embedded cover); once probed its
    DLNA profile is sent with the stream.
  - An opened folder remembers its number of entries, reported as
    childCount while its mtime is unchanged.
  - Photos with a known resolution get /Resized/ and EXIF /Thumbnails/
    URLs again.
 .
 The metadata extractors in metadata.c are split so Probe*Metadata() fill
 a struct media_info instead of inserting into the database; database mode
 is unchanged. They and image_utils.c keep static state, so all probing
 runs in one worker thread and browses wait for it with tickets.
 enable_thumbnail defaults to yes in live folder mode, and live folder
 titles are full file names, extension included.
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-10-21
